<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Audio versions of endjin blog posts, published as a Podcasting 2.0 feed.

  Authored rather than mirrored: endjin publishes an audio version of many posts under
  /assets/podcast/, but no podcast RSS feed of its own, so this file assembles real assets into the feed
  a podcast host would serve. Every enclosure URL, media type and byte count below is real and was
  checked with a HEAD request.

  The asset name comes from the post title, not from its slug, and cannot be derived from one. The first
  episode is the example: the slug is genai-reality-check-new-instrument-same-orchestra, and the file is
  2026-05-14-the-genai-reality-check-new-Instrument-same-orchestra.mp3 — an extra "the-" and a capital I.
  Read the <audio> element off the post; do not construct the URL.

  The namespace is https://podcastindex.org/namespace/1.0 — https, and matched exactly. A feed declaring
  the http:// form silently yields no extension at all, because discovery compares the namespace URI
  rather than the prefix.

  The podcast:txt element with purpose="applepodcastsverify" is the reason this extension matters. A
  survey of live feeds found the Apple ownership token delivered that way by 21 publishers and as
  itunes:applepodcastsverify by 26, so a library reading only the iTunes form serves about half of the
  publishers who set one, and loses the other half's claim to their own show.
-->
